.Dd June 17, 2026
.Dt ZDOTS-O2-QUERY 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm zdots-o2-query
.Nd read runtime insight back from OpenObserve into a session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the read side of the intelligence loop
.Pq Z-135 :
it queries the local OpenObserve backend for recent errors, slow spans,
failures, per-service activity, log searches, or a single trace, as compact
tables or JSON an agent can reason over.
.Pp
Read-only and local-only
.Pq loopback O2 .
Credentials come from the Keychain, never the command line, so it is safe on
the work machine.
Telemetry is scrubbed at the ingest edge; a light defense-in-depth scrub runs
on read and can be skipped with
.Fl -no-scrub .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width failures
.It Cm errors
Recent ERROR/FATAL logs.
.It Cm slow
Slowest spans over a threshold
.Pq Fl -ms .
.It Cm failures
Error-status spans.
.It Cm service
Activity grouped by service and severity.
.It Cm logs
General log search
.Pq Fl -grep .
.It Cm trace Ar id
All spans and logs for one trace.
.It Cm sql Fl -type Ar logs | traces Ar query
Read-only SQL escape hatch.
.It Cm streams
List OpenObserve streams.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -since Ar dur
Time window
.Pq Li 30s , 15m , 2h , 1d ; default Li 1h .
.It Fl n , Fl -limit Ar n
Row limit
.Pq default 20 .
.It Fl -json
Machine-readable output.
.It Fl -no-scrub
Skip the defense-in-depth scrub pass.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_O2_ENDPOINT
.It Ev ZDOTS_O2_ENDPOINT
OpenObserve endpoint. Defaults to
.Li http://127.0.0.1:5080 .
.El
.Sh PHI SAFETY
Read-only and loopback-bound; credentials are read from the Keychain. If the
defense-in-depth scrub ever trips a suppress-flagged value, that signals an
ingest-scrub gap, not normal operation.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zdots-observability 7 ,
.Xr openobserve-ctl 8
